<title>USA: Browning-Ferris charges reflect shift.</title>
<headline>Browning-Ferris charges reflect shift.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Browning-Ferris Industries Inc said the special charges taken in the fourth quarter are part of a strategic shift by the company from an emphasis on external growth to an emphasis on internal growth.</p>
<p>Success will be measured by cash flow and return on gross assets, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;While fiscal 1996 results were disappointing, we believe that the revised financial goals announced last week, and other steps taken, will more closely align the company's performance with our shareholders' interests,&quot; chief executive Bruce Ranck said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;These revised goals emphasize cash flow in excess of the weighted average cost of capital as BFI's highest financial priority,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
